Z||000019||saleenfiero||08-28-2001||05:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Brandon86SE:<BR><B>Hey Saleen, why didn't I ever see that Fiero?  I lived in Medicine Hat for 2 years and just moved to Calgary 10 months ago.  I've had my baby for almost 2 years now, and thought I'd seen all the ones in Medicine Hat.  Mine was one of the 2 gold ones.  The better one.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Brandon:  Well I was always around somewhere driving.  I'm thinking I remember your car.  Did you have a wing on yours?<P>Everyone:  The Saleen wing really give the fiero a neat silhouette.  Sort of a raked appearance on the coupes.  And like I said, mine was a dead on fit on the decklid.<P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Philphine||08-28-2001||05:31 PM||||saleen's right. mine came while i was at work and i saw it in the morning. placed it on the lid and didn't really have to do any finagling to get it to fit. i drilled holes and had it on in about 1/2 hour.<P>i'm putting an f40 mustang wing on another fiero and it fits almost the same. maybe i'll put a new style saleen wing on my gt just for the fun of having mustang wing on all my fiero's (except the indy).||||reg||1
